<title>BRAZIL: Brazil sells virtually all coffee in stock auction.</title>
<headline>Brazil sells virtually all coffee in stock auction.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian government sold 62,103 60-kg bags of coffee or 88.99 percent of its auction today of 69,783 bags of stocks, said an official from the Banco do Brasil which held the electronic auction.</p>
<p>Prices ranged between 96 and 118.15 reais ($97.92 and $120.51) a bag, with total income from the sale 6.30 million reais ($6.43 million), the official said.</p>
<p>The next auction is scheduled to be held on November 20 and roasters have already asked for the size of future sales to be nearer to the current limit of 200,000 bags.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
